<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 13 November, from 1002 to 2015.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1002 <span class="tih-ago">1,024 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Æthelred II orders the St Brice's Day massacre of Danes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Æthelred the Unready ordered the killing of Danish men in England. Victims reputedly included the sister of Sweyn Forkbeard, who launched repeated invasions and took the English crown in 1013.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/scotland" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scotland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1093 <span class="tih-ago">933 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Malcolm III of Scotland is killed at Alnwick</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Malcolm III was killed in an ambush while besieging Alnwick Castle in Northumberland, together with his eldest son. A succession struggle followed in Scotland.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/quebec" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quebec.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1775 <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">American forces occupy Montreal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Continental troops under Richard Montgomery entered Montreal unopposed during the invasion of Canada. The campaign collapsed after the failed assault on Quebec City at the end of the year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hungary" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hungary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1918 <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Charles withdraws from Hungarian affairs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Eckartsau, Charles I renounced any part in Hungary's government, two days after a similar declaration for Austria. Habsburg rule over Austria-Hungary was effectively at an end.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2015 <span class="tih-ago">11 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Coordinated terrorist attacks kill 130 in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Islamic State gunmen and suicide bombers attacked the Bataclan concert hall, cafés and the Stade de France. It was the deadliest attack in France since the Second World War, and a state of emergency followed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
